# A payload-free variant of an enum whose other variants carry a payload
# borrows one static box per variant instead of allocating one: a million of
# them in a list cost under 24 bytes each in resident memory, where a block
# apiece made them about 50. The program also writes new variants over
# payload-free ones through a write window and an index, copies and drops
# them, generic instances included, and panics when a value reads wrong or
# the peak RSS grows with the round count.
# The web target is not Jet-hosted yet (E2104), so no web step.
fixture: PayloadFreeVariantsAllocateNothing.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
env: JETPACK_ENV=1
step: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
step aot: built
stdin: null
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = payload_free_variants_allocate_nothing.stdout.expected
stderr: empty
step: jet run main.jet
stdin: null
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = payload_free_variants_allocate_nothing.stdout.expected
stderr: empty
